    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κίμωλος</span></b> , [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], ἡ</span>, <u>Cimolus</u>, an
		island in the Cyclades:—Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κῐμώλιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἰσχάδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Amphis
					40
				</span></i>
			: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κῐμωλία</span></b>  (with or
			without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>), ἡ, <i>Cimolian earth</i>, a white clay, like
			<i>fuller's earth</i>, used in baths and barbers' shops, and in
			medicine, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				713
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.5.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.156
			</span></i>.</div>
